From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LS1046A integration <maintainers@vyos.net>
Date: Mon, 25 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] http-api: add Model Context Protocol (MCP) server (default off)

Mounts an MCP Streamable-HTTP endpoint at /mcp/ inside the existing
vyos-http-api-server (FastAPI). Exposes operational commands, config
read/modify, image management, and schema introspection as MCP tools,
resources and prompts for AI-agent integration.

Config: `set service https api mcp mode <read-only|read-write>` and
`set service https api mcp introspection`. The node is absent by default,
so the endpoint ships DORMANT (off) until explicitly configured.

The mcp SDK and its Python deps (httpx, httpx-sse, pydantic-settings,
sse-starlette) are provided by the vyos-http-api-tools virtualenv rebuilt
with mcp==1.8.1 (see bin/ci-build-http-api-tools.sh), NOT a system
python3-mcp package -- so the upstream fork's debian/control python3-mcp
Depends line is intentionally omitted here.

Origin: mihakralj/vyos-1x branch T9030-mcp.
---
